<article class="env-lemma" id="0DYW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DYW">Lemma <span data-tag="0DYW">93.9.6</span>.</a> In Example <a href="/tag/0DY7" data-tag="0DY7">93.9.1</a> let $X$ be a scheme over $k$. Let $U \subset X$ be an open subscheme. There is a natural functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{D}\! \mathit{ef}_ X \longrightarrow \mathcal{D}\! \mathit{ef}_ U  \]
</div>
  <p> of deformation categories. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Given a deformation of $X$ we can take the corresponding open of it to get a deformation of $U$. We omit the details. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>